rb_parallel_cos"], "convention": "the bus counts as approximately parallel to the curb, and so not projecting across the adjacent travel lane, where the absolute cosine between its heading (kin.heading) and the designated direction (st.lane_direction) of a travel region it occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), whose carriers run along the curb, is at least p.curb_parallel_cos, the bus-stop alignment tolerance of transit stop design guidance", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a bus and not a tour bus; at the observation it is at rest (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance) with a door open (sig.door_open), and its footprint overlaps a bus stop, bus stand, passenger loading zone or origin or destination point (st.transit_stop; st.curb_zone of kind bus_stop or passenger_loading) on a street (st.highway).", "obligation": "Some road edge lies on the subject's right (prim.region_lateral_offset negative) at a ground distance from the subject's body outline (st.region_geometry) of at most the stated eighteen inches; and for some travel region the subject occupies, the absolute cosine between the subject's heading and that region's designated direction is at least p.curb_parallel_cos.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.curb_parallel_cos"], "narrowings": [{"span": "c1", "why": "'The operator of a bus' is read through the bus's own controlled motion, whoever or whatever is at the controls.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "c3", "why": "A bus stand and an origin or destination point are read through the posted bus zone on the road (st.curb_zone kind bus_stop), the posting being the evidence of their designation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "c5", "why": "The purpose of loading or unloading passengers or baggage is read through the halted bus having a door open.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "c6", "why": "The right-hand front wheel is read through the bus's body outline: the wheel lies within the outline at its right side, so the body's ground distance to the curb on the right, with the bus parallel to the curb, is the wheel's distance less the tyre's small inset from the body side; a wheel's own position is not in the vocabulary. A bus whose body is within the stated distance but whose wheel is beyond it by less than that inset is read as compliant.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "c7", "why": "'so as not to unduly impede the movement of other vehicular traffic' is read only through the bus's alignment with the curb (and its curb distance in c6): the movement of actual other traffic is not read.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A transit bus comes to rest in a st.curb_zone of kind bus_stop on a street, its curb-side door open, with its body 1.5 m from the road edge on its right and its heading along the lane direction."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A transit bus comes to rest in a st.curb_zone of kind bus_stop, door open, its body 0.2 m from the road edge on its right and its heading along the lane direction."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A transit bus drives through a bus-stop curb zone without halting, all doors closed."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "masked": ["st.region_geometry"], "narrative": "A transit bus comes to rest in a bus-stop curb zone with its door open; the source maps the road edge without its outline, so the distance from the bus's body to the curb is unknown."}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A transit bus comes to rest in a bus-stop curb zone with its door open, its front body 0.2 m from the road edge on its right but its heading thirty degrees off the lane direction, its rear swung out into the lane."}], "literals": [{"span": "c6", "text": "eighteen inches", "value": 18, "unit": "in"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source's kinematic channel"}, {"name": "p.curb_parallel_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.97, "convention": "cosine of the largest angle (about fourteen degrees) between a stopped bus's heading and its carrier's designated direction, in either sense, at which the bus counts as approximately parallel to the curb", "source": "transit agency bus stop design guidance on bus alignment at the curb"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}

